  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "Only the controllable events that determine task progression—claim_<color>, pick_up_object, drop_object, search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone—were included. Uncontrollable observation events for object and zone visibility/arbitration (<color>_object_visible, <color>_object_not_visible, <color>_object_reached, <color>_zone_visible, <color>_zone_not_visible, <color>_zone_reached, received_claim_<color>) are necessary as state triggers. Other events, e.g., low-level motion commands and obstacle events, are excluded as their handling is enforced by separate fixed automata.",
    "transition_design": "The automaton starts in unclaimed object search (obj_search), with loops on search_object for continuous searching. Observing a specific color transitions to color-claim state (e.g., red_claim), where only claim_<color> or received_claim_<color> is enabled—the latter reverting to search if the claim fails. Success allows approach_object self-loops in object-approach states, advancing to pickup only on <color>_object_reached. Loss of visibility returns to a color-specific object-search state, with reacquisition moving back to approach. After pick_up_object, the robot enters zone search, self-looping on search_zone and responding to matching zone visibility. Transition to approach_zone occurs on visibility, with loss bringing the state back to search; both zone states progress to the drop state on <color>_zone_reached. Only drop_object is valid at the drop state, which is marked as complete. This system branches by observed color and provides a complete single-color delivery cycle for any of red, green, or blue.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
